{"seq":7,"id":"01M8E44HZWHJGJ51TFKVMQERFZ","cdr":"CDR-0003","attempt":"CDR-0003-A1","type":"agent.result","actor":{"kind":"agent","id":"test_author","adapter":"claude-sonnet"},"at":"2026-11-27T09:07:15.580Z","payload":{"role":"test_author","adapter":"claude-sonnet","result_sha256":"78e08bea048e1090d20332631af61e478f71c523988098063cf159a42da186ee","result":{"tests":[{"path":"scripts/design-md-gen.cdr0003.test.mjs","covers_criterion":"1 (byte-for-byte equality; import writes no file) and 2 (gen:design-md script; running it reproduces DESIGN.md). Also the constraints that values come from the sources and that missing source content makes the generator fail."},{"path":"scripts/design-md.cdr0003.test.mjs","covers_criterion":"3 (section order), 4 (colour roles and accent registry), 5 (typography, spacing, radii, control height), 6 (depth), 7 (signature components and bezel card), 8 (motion), 9 (effects), 10 (do and do-not lists), 11 (no dates or owner annotations), 12 (README row), 13 (package files list)"}],"run_command":"node --test scripts/design-md.cdr0003.test.mjs scripts/design-md-gen.cdr0003.test.mjs","notes":"I did not run the tests because I had no shell. By reading the code, I expect every test to fail on the current code, since the generator, DESIGN.md, the npm script and the README row are all missing.\n\nThe tests require this DESIGN.md format. The CDR does not fix it.\n1. **Sections:** there are nine `## ` headings, in order. Their titles match, in turn: brand or voice; colour; typography; spacing; depth; signature or component; motion; effect; and a title starting with \"Do\" or containing \"do not\" / \"don't\". Extra `###` headings are fine. Fenced code is ignored when headings are read.\n2. **Colour roles:** use Markdown tables with Light, Dark, High contrast and Purpose (or \"Use\") header columns. The first cell names `--sl-\u003crole\u003e`.\n   - **Roles:** every non-`code-*` role in `neutrals.json` `products.default` and in `tokens.themes`, plus `--sl-accent-default` (all three themes).\n   - **Values:** print raw token values, including the `oklch(...)` string for light `text-on-accent`. Whitespace, backticks and case are ignored.\n3. **Accent registry:** it sits in the colour section, with one line per product giving the id and both its light and dark hex. `daos` shows the resolved default accents.\n4. **Token lines:** in typography, spacing and motion, one line holds both the full token name (`--sl-font-*`, `--sl-text-*`, `--sl-space-*`, `--sl-radius-*`, `--sl-motion-*`) and its full raw value. This covers every key, including `spring` and `pill`. The control height sits on a spacing-section line that also says \"control\" or \"height\".\n5. **Entries:** each depth recipe, signature component and effect family has a line starting with its name. That line can be a `###` heading, list item, table row or paragraph, optionally bold, backticked or prefixed with \"The\". The names are:\n   - **Depth:** Tile, Flat tile, Island, Key, Sunk, Float, Cast.\n   - **Components:** Wordmark, Eyebrow, Tag, Inversion band, Keycap, Tile, Bezel card.\n   - **Effects:** Glitch, Aurora, Glass, Goo.\n\n   An entry runs until the next of these labels, so don't start other lines in the same section with those words. The bezel card entry must say \"chosen\" and \"not shipped\" or \"not yet shipped\"; no other component entry may say \"not shipped\". Each effect entry contains its meaning phrase from the \"X means *...*\" sentence in design-language.md.\n6. **Motion rules:** the section mentions reduced motion, page-load choreography and the dither.\n7. **Do lists:** the last section has `### Do` and `### Do not` headings (`##` to `####` are accepted; \"Don't\" and a trailing \"list\" also work). A `## Do ...` heading must also serve as the ninth section's start. The do-not list contains each flavour.md trait name word for word. The do list keeps the key words of all 12 brand traits.\n8. **No history:** the output has no ISO dates, \"owner ruling/amendment/decision/override/approval/pick\", \"(owner\", \"owner,\" or \"owner:\", \"amended\" or \"amendment\", or \"until/since [ui-kit] X.Y\". This also applies to quoted flavour.md rule cells.\n9. **README row:** it has the form ``| `DESIGN.md` | description |``.\n\nThe generator tests run on a temporary copy containing only `package.json`, `sondalab.tokens.json`, `docs/`, `scripts/` and `packages/ui-kit/`, so the generator must not read anything outside these.\n- **Source changes:** the tests change some space, radius, text and motion tokens. They replace every `32px` with `36px` in both copies of design-language.md, and add a new flavour.md do-not row. All of these must show up in the output without an error, so don't require a hand-written entry for each do-not trait, and don't pin 32 anywhere.\n- **Broken sources:** the script must exit non-zero and leave DESIGN.md untouched if every `32px` is gone, the do-not-converge section is gone, or `shared.motion` is gone.\n- **Run-directly check:** `buildDesignMd()` must return a string synchronously for the byte-for-byte test.\n\nThe tests don't check the wording of the brand summary or of the reasons beside rules, or which source wins when flavour.md and design-language.md disagree, so review those by hand."}},"cost":{"tokens_in":12,"tokens_out":20121,"tokens_cache_write":94462,"tokens_cache_read":289989,"seconds":141.629456791,"usd":0.6080809},"signer":"ads-team:marcello.barile@gmail.com","prev_hash":"013bb761cacc90d82bf4a85609fe5a1749d19c1641b08dfec683a823f9b67228","hash":"195335a1bb42131011e4c35df65d2f6a7c860fee7c695600234467092fb6bbf3","sig":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgt+9LVHCb4CLBAIrBcP4iIkhhc+\nSCDbAr1oNRi9kG2bAAAAAJYWRzLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1l\nZDI1NTE5AAAAQNF3/HBWul/FITIO0l+V4VVXgM8RKS3EfcW9kbOOPl0ZRkeuwh+pnIKL6L\nGQE24HU5KSfA9SyOZXEPrPBBB+GAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----\n"}
